    "title": "Special Weather Statement by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "29 minutes ago Check NWS updates here\nEffective: 2025-09-04 00:02:00 EDT Expires: 2025-09-04 00:30:00 EDT Urgency: Expected Severity: Moderate Certainty: Observed Instruction: If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building. Target Area: Marion; Hancock; Henry; Johnson; Shelby; Rush; Bartholomew At 1201 AM EDT, Doppler radar was tracking strong thunderstorms along a line extending from 9 miles north of Greenfield to 7 miles southwest of Franklin. Movement was southeast at 45 mph.\nHAZARD...Wind gusts of 50 to 55 mph.\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured objects.\nLocations impacted include... Indianapolis, Shelbyville, Greenwood, Franklin, Greenfield, New Whiteland, Cumberland, Edinburgh, Whiteland, Bargersville, Knightstown, Hope, New Palestine, Flat Rock, Geneva, Morristown, Carthage, Spiceland, Shirley, and Wilkinson.\nThis includes the following highways... Interstate 65 between mile markers 81 and 99. Interstate 70 between mile markers 96 and 126. Interstate 74 between mile markers 97 and 122.",
